You are tasked with creating a program that analyzes the distribution of Java package names within a given codebase. The program should read a Java source file and count the occurrences of unique package names. A package name is considered unique if it has not been encountered before in the source file. The program should then output the unique package names along with their respective occurrence counts.

Write a function or method `packageDistribution` that takes a string representing the Java source code as input and returns a map of unique package names to their occurrence counts.

For example, given the following Java source code snippet:
```java
/*
 * This is a sample Java source file
 */
package com.github.harbby.gadtry.graph.impl;

import java.util.*;

public class SampleClass {
    // class implementation
}
```
The function `packageDistribution` should return a map with the following key-value pairs:
```
{
  "com.github.harbby.gadtry.graph.impl": 1,
  "java.util": 1
}
```
Note that the package name "java.util" is also included, even though it is a standard Java package.

Assumptions:
- The input Java source code will be well-formed and syntactically correct.
- Package names will follow the standard Java package naming conventions.
- The input source code may contain multiple class definitions and package declarations.

```java
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.regex.Matcher;
import java.util.regex.Pattern;

public class PackageAnalyzer {
    public static Map<String, Integer> packageDistribution(String sourceCode) {
        Map<String, Integer> packageCounts = new HashMap<>();
        Pattern packagePattern = Pattern.compile("package\\s+([\\w.]+);");
        Matcher matcher = packagePattern.matcher(sourceCode);

        while (matcher.find()) {
            String packageName = matcher.group(1);
            packageCounts.put(packageName, packageCounts.getOrDefault(packageName, 0) + 1);
        }

        return packageCounts;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String javaSourceCode = "/*\n * This is a sample Java source file\n */\npackage com.github.harbby.gadtry.graph.impl;\n\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class SampleClass {\n    // class implementation\n}";
        Map<String, Integer> distribution = packageDistribution(javaSourceCode);
        for (Map.Entry<String, Integer> entry : distribution.entrySet()) {
            System.out.println(entry.getKey() + ": " + entry.getValue());
        }
    }
}
```

The `packageDistribution` method uses a regular expression to match package declarations in the input Java source code. It then populates a map with the unique package names and their occurrence counts. The main method demonstrates the usage of the `packageDistribution` method with a sample Java source code and prints the package distribution to the console.

