public boolean hasPrefix(byte[] prefix, byte[] receivedData, int length) {
    // Check if the received data is at least as long as the prefix
    if (receivedData.length < prefix.length) {
        return false;  // The received data is shorter than the prefix, so it cannot have the prefix
    }

    // Check each byte of the prefix against the corresponding byte in the received data
    for (int i = 0; i < prefix.length; i++) {
        if (receivedData[i] != prefix[i]) {
            return false;  // Mismatch found, the received data does not have the specified prefix
        }
    }

    return true;  // All bytes of the prefix match the corresponding bytes in the received data
}
```

The `hasPrefix` method first checks if the received data is at least as long as the prefix. If the received data is shorter than the prefix, it cannot contain the prefix, so the method returns `false`. If the received data is long enough, the method then iterates through each byte of the prefix and compares it with the corresponding byte in the received data. If any mismatch is found, the method returns `false`. If all bytes of the prefix match the corresponding bytes in the received data, the method returns `true`, indicating that the received data has the specified prefix.

