You are tasked with implementing a custom annotation processor for a Java application. The annotation `@WithSpan` is used to mark methods that should be wrapped with a timing span for performance monitoring. Your goal is to create a processor that will generate the necessary code to start and end a timing span around the annotated methods.

Your annotation processor should generate the following code for each method annotated with `@WithSpan`:
```java
Span span = PerformanceMonitor.startSpan("methodName");
try {
    // original method body
} finally {
    PerformanceMonitor.endSpan(span);
}
```
Where `"methodName"` is the name of the annotated method.

Write a Java annotation processor that processes classes and generates the required code for methods annotated with `@WithSpan`.

```java
import javax.annotation.processing.AbstractProcessor;
import javax.annotation.processing.RoundEnvironment;
import javax.annotation.processing.SupportedAnnotationTypes;
import javax.lang.model.element.Element;
import javax.lang.model.element.ElementKind;
import javax.lang.model.element.ExecutableElement;
import javax.lang.model.element.TypeElement;
import javax.lang.model.type.DeclaredType;
import javax.lang.model.type.TypeMirror;
import javax.tools.Diagnostic;
import javax.tools.JavaFileObject;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.io.PrintWriter;
import java.util.Set;

@SupportedAnnotationTypes("WithSpan")
public class WithSpanProcessor extends AbstractProcessor {

    @Override
    public boolean process(Set<? extends TypeElement> annotations, RoundEnvironment roundEnv) {
        for (Element element : roundEnv.getElementsAnnotatedWith(WithSpan.class)) {
            if (element.getKind() == ElementKind.METHOD) {
                ExecutableElement method = (ExecutableElement) element;
                TypeElement classElement = (TypeElement) method.getEnclosingElement();
                String className = classElement.getQualifiedName().toString();
                String methodName = method.getSimpleName().toString();

                try {
                    JavaFileObject fileObject = processingEnv.getFiler().createSourceFile(className + "WithSpanProcessor");
                    try (PrintWriter writer = new PrintWriter(fileObject.openWriter())) {
                        writer.println("Span span = PerformanceMonitor.startSpan(\"" + methodName + "\");");
                        writer.println("try {");
                        writer.println("    " + className + "." + methodName + "();");
                        writer.println("} finally {");
                        writer.println("    PerformanceMonitor.endSpan(span);");
                        writer.println("}");
                    }
                } catch (IOException e) {
                    processingEnv.getMessager().printMessage(Diagnostic.Kind.ERROR, "Error creating file: " + e.getMessage());
                }
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```
This annotation processor processes classes and generates the required code for methods annotated with `@WithSpan`. It creates a new source file for each annotated method, containing the code to start and end a timing span around the method's original body.

