public class TimeInterval {
    private String startTime;
    private static final int DURATION_HOURS = 1;

    public void setStartTime(final String startTime) {
        if (isValidTime(startTime)) {
            this.startTime = startTime;
        } else {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid start time format. Please use HH:MM format.");
        }
    }

    public String getEndTime() {
        if (startTime == null) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Start time has not been set.");
        }
        String[] parts = startTime.split(":");
        int startHour = Integer.parseInt(parts[0]);
        int startMinute = Integer.parseInt(parts[1]);
        int endHour = (startHour + DURATION_HOURS) % 24;
        int endMinute = startMinute;
        return String.format("%02d:%02d", endHour, endMinute);
    }

    private boolean isValidTime(String time) {
        return time.matches("^([01]?[0-9]|2[0-3]):[0-5][0-9]$");
    }
}
```

This `TimeInterval` class ensures that the start time is set in the correct format and provides the end time based on the predefined duration. The `isValidTime` method uses a regular expression to validate the time format. The `getEndTime` method calculates the end time based on the start time and the predefined duration, handling the wrap-around from 23:59 to 00:00 appropriately.

