Write a method `removeOldGames` that takes the maximum age of games in hours as a parameter and removes all games older than this threshold. Return the number of games removed as a response.

```java
import com.google.common.collect.ImmutableMap;
import javax.ws.rs.core.Response;

public class GameRepository {
    private List<Game> games; // Assume games is a list of Game objects

    public Response removeOldGames(int maxAgeInHours) {
        int gamesRemoved = 0;
        Iterator<Game> iterator = games.iterator();
        long currentTimeMillis = System.currentTimeMillis();

        while (iterator.hasNext()) {
            Game game = iterator.next();
            long gameAgeInHours = (currentTimeMillis - game.getCreationTime()) / (1000 * 60 * 60); // Convert milliseconds to hours

            if (gameAgeInHours > maxAgeInHours) {
                iterator.remove();
                gamesRemoved++;
            }
        }

        return Response.ok(ImmutableMap.of("removed", gamesRemoved)).build();
    }
}
```

In the solution, we iterate through the list of games and calculate the age of each game in hours based on the current time and the game's creation time. If the game's age exceeds the `maxAgeInHours`, we remove it from the list and increment the `gamesRemoved` counter. Finally, we return the number of games removed as a response using `ImmutableMap`.

