    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Create a JobScheduler with a pool size of 5 threads
        JobScheduler jobScheduler = new JobScheduler(5);

        // Submit some sample jobs to the scheduler
        for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
            int jobId = i + 1;
            jobScheduler.submitJob(() -> {
                System.out.println("Executing job " + jobId + " on thread " + Thread.currentThread().getName());
                try {
                    Thread.sleep(1000); // Simulate job execution time
                } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                    Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                }
            });
        }

        // Shut down the scheduler and wait for all submitted jobs to be completed
        jobScheduler.shutdown();
    }
}
```

In this solution, the `JobScheduler` class initializes a thread pool with a specified number of threads and provides methods to submit jobs for execution and shut down the thread pool. The `Main` class demonstrates how to use the `JobScheduler` to submit jobs and ensure their completion before shutting down the scheduler.

