- A method is considered to be marked with the `@Deprecated` annotation if it has the `@Deprecated` annotation directly preceding its declaration.
- A method is considered to be missing the `@deprecated` Javadoc tag if it has a Javadoc comment (i.e., starts with `/**`) but does not contain the `@deprecated` tag within the comment.

