```java
public int countUniqueSDKInitializations(String codeSnippet) {
    Set<String> uniqueSDKInitializations = new HashSet<>();
    String[] lines = codeSnippet.split("\\r?\\n");

    for (String line : lines) {
        String methodName = extractMethodName(line);
        if (methodName != null && methodName.startsWith("init")) {
            uniqueSDKInitializations.add(methodName);
        }
    }

    return uniqueSDKInitializations.size();
}

private String extractMethodName(String line) {
    String methodName = null;
    int startIndex = line.indexOf('(');
    if (startIndex != -1) {
        int spaceIndex = line.lastIndexOf(' ', startIndex);
        if (spaceIndex != -1) {
            methodName = line.substring(spaceIndex + 1, startIndex);
        }
    }
    return methodName;
}
```

In the solution, the `countUniqueSDKInitializations` function first splits the code snippet into individual lines and then iterates through each line to extract the method names. It identifies the SDK initialization calls based on the method names starting with "init" and adds them to a set to ensure uniqueness. Finally, it returns the count of unique SDK initializations found in the code snippet.

