public static int maximumPerimeterTriangle(int[] sticks) {
    Arrays.sort(sticks); // Sort the sticks in non-decreasing order

    for (int i = sticks.length - 1; i >= 2; i--) {
        if (sticks[i] < sticks[i - 1] + sticks[i - 2]) {
            return sticks[i] + sticks[i - 1] + sticks[i - 2]; // Return the maximum perimeter
        }
    }
    return -1; // If no triangle can be formed, return -1
}
```

The solution first sorts the array of sticks in non-decreasing order. Then, it iterates through the sorted array from the end, checking if it is possible to form a triangle with the current stick and the two preceding sticks. If a valid triangle can be formed, the function returns the maximum perimeter. If no valid triangle can be formed, the function returns -1.

