public class EnergyStorageComponent {
    private int maxStoredPower;
    private int currentStoredPower;
    private int maxExtract;
    private int maxReceive;

    public EnergyStorageComponent(int maxStoredPower, int maxExtract, int maxReceive) {
        this.maxStoredPower = maxStoredPower;
        this.maxExtract = maxExtract;
        this.maxReceive = maxReceive;
        this.currentStoredPower = 0;
    }

    public int extractEnergy(int maxExtract, boolean simulate) {
        int extractedEnergy = Math.min(maxExtract, currentStoredPower);
        if (!simulate) {
            currentStoredPower -= extractedEnergy;
        }
        return extractedEnergy;
    }

    public int receiveEnergy(int maxReceive, boolean simulate) {
        int spaceAvailable = maxStoredPower - currentStoredPower;
        int receivedEnergy = Math.min(maxReceive, spaceAvailable);
        if (!simulate) {
            currentStoredPower += receivedEnergy;
        }
        return receivedEnergy;
    }
}
```
In the solution, the `EnergyStorageComponent` class is implemented with the specified properties and methods. The `extractEnergy` method ensures that the requested amount of energy is extracted, limited by the available stored power. The `receiveEnergy` method ensures that the requested amount of energy is received, limited by the available storage space. Both methods also handle the simulation flag to indicate whether the operations should be simulated or actually performed.

