public String getHint(String secret, String guess) {
    int bulls = 0, cows = 0;
    int[] numbers = new int[10]; // Array to store the frequency of digits

    for (int i = 0; i < secret.length(); i++) {
        char s = secret.charAt(i);
        char g = guess.charAt(i);
        if (s == g) {
            bulls++;
        } else {
            if (numbers[s - '0'] < 0) cows++; // If the frequency of s in secret is negative, it means it has been guessed in the past
            if (numbers[g - '0'] > 0) cows++; // If the frequency of g in guess is positive, it means it has been present in the secret
            numbers[s - '0']++; // Increment the frequency of s in secret
            numbers[g - '0']--; // Decrement the frequency of g in guess
        }
    }
    return bulls + "A" + cows + "B";
}
```

The `getHint` function iterates through the secret and guess strings, counting the bulls and cows as per the game rules. It uses an array `numbers` to store the frequency of digits encountered in the strings. If a digit is a bull, it increments the bull count; otherwise, it checks if the digit has been guessed before and updates the cow count accordingly. Finally, it returns the count of bulls and cows in the required format.

