public static int countWaysToReachTop(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) {
        return n;
    }
    int[] ways = new int[n + 1];
    ways[0] = 1;
    ways[1] = 1;
    for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
        ways[i] = ways[i - 1] + ways[i - 2];
    }
    return ways[n];
}
```
The solution uses dynamic programming to efficiently calculate the total number of ways to reach the top of the staircase. It initializes an array `ways` to store the number of ways to reach each step. It then iterates through the steps, calculating the number of ways to reach each step based on the number of ways to reach the previous two steps. Finally, it returns the total number of ways to reach the top of the staircase.

