import org.neo4j.driver.*;

public List<String> getSourceNodeAcronyms(List<String> designs) {
    List<String> acronyms = new ArrayList<>();

    try (Driver driver = GraphDatabase.driver("bolt://localhost:7687", AuthTokens.basic("username", "password"))) {
        try (Session session = driver.session()) {
            String query = "MATCH (s)-[]->(d:NeoDesign) " +
                           "WHERE d.name IN $designs " +
                           "RETURN s.acronym";

            Result result = session.run(query, Values.parameters("designs", designs));

            while (result.hasNext()) {
                Record record = result.next();
                acronyms.add(record.get("s.acronym").asString());
            }
        }
    }

    return acronyms;
}
```

In this solution, the function establishes a connection to the Neo4j database using the official Neo4j Java driver. It constructs a Cypher query to match the source nodes connected to the specified design elements and retrieves their acronyms. The function then returns a list of acronyms corresponding to the source nodes connected to the given design elements.

