public class Node {
    private String graphId;
    private Map<String, Object> metadata;

    public void setGraphId(String graphId) {
        this.graphId = graphId;
    }

    public void setMetadata(Map<String, Object> metadata) {
        this.metadata = metadata;
    }

    public boolean validateUpdateOperation(String graphId, Node node, String validationMode, String versionKey) {
        if (!graphId.equals(node.graphId)) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Graph ID mismatch");
        }

        if (metadata == null || !metadata.containsKey("versionKey")) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Metadata does not contain version key");
        }

        String currentVersionKey = (String) metadata.get("versionKey");

        if (validationMode.equals("STRICT")) {
            return versionKey.equals(currentVersionKey);
        } else if (validationMode.equals("NON_STRICT")) {
            return versionKey.compareTo(currentVersionKey) >= 0;
        } else {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid validation mode");
        }
    }
}
```

In the `validateUpdateOperation` method, we first check if the provided graph ID matches the node's graph ID. Then, we ensure that the node's metadata contains a "versionKey" entry. Depending on the validation mode, we compare the provided version key with the current version key of the node to determine the validity of the update operation. If the validation mode is "STRICT", an exact match is required, while in "NON_STRICT" mode, a comparison based on lexicographical order is performed. If the validation mode is neither "STRICT" nor "NON_STRICT", an exception is thrown.

