class CustomStack {
    private int[] stack;
    private int top;

    public CustomStack(int maxSize) {
        stack = new int[maxSize];
        top = -1;
    }

    public void push(int x) {
        if (top < stack.length - 1) {
            top++;
            stack[top] = x;
        }
    }

    public int pop() {
        if (top >= 0) {
            int val = stack[top];
            top--;
            return val;
        }
        return -1;
    }

    public void increment(int k, int val) {
        int min = Math.min(k, top + 1);
        for (int i = 0; i < min; i++) {
            stack[i] += val;
        }
    }
}
```

The `CustomStack` class is implemented with the required methods to simulate the behavior of a stack with additional functionality. The `push` method adds an element to the top of the stack, the `pop` method removes the top element, and the `increment` method increments the bottom `k` elements of the stack by `val`. If there are less than `k` elements in the stack, it increments all elements.

